# component: checkbox
# decisions: A11Y-19, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-12, FOC-5, FOC-6, FRM-15
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-3
#     focus-visible:ring-ring/50` and the `aria-invalid` halo rings are removed. `base.css` owns
#     the one `:focus-visible` outline and `outline-none` would suppress it.
#   FOC-5: the invalid tint and its checked counterpart become
#     `not-focus:aria-invalid:border-destructive` and
#     `not-focus:aria-invalid:aria-checked:border-primary`, so focus outranks the error colour.
#   FOC-12: the three `group-has-[:focus-visible]/field-label:` rules are removed. They exist to
#     cancel the control's ring while the choice CARD is ringed; this system rings the control, and
#     the card's ring is removed in field.tsx by the same decision.
#   A11Y-19: the indicator renders through Base UI's `render` callback and draws `MinusIcon` when
#     the state is indeterminate, `CheckIcon` otherwise (upstream always draws the check, so the
#     mixed state looked identical to checked). `MinusIcon` joins the lucide import.
#   FRM-15: `disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50` become `data-disabled:…`. Base UI
#     renders the root as a `<span>`, which `:disabled` never matches, so upstream's control dimmed
#     only inside a disabled Field; Base UI sets `data-disabled` on the root.
#   shape: ours — `shape?: "square" | "circle"` (default square) adds `rounded-full` for a
#     round check that marks a task done; square stays for selection and form fields.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
